# Hazard Pressure 5 of 10 — rescue is a distance budget.
# Terrain and placement share one grid, so the board is what it looks like.
#   .  open        #  wall        O  pit        ^  spikes      H  high ground
#   A  Player A deploy slot       B  Player B deploy slot
#   any other letter = an enemy declared by a 'spawn' line below
#
# A unit that falls in clings until the end of the round AFTER the one it fell in, and only
# an ADJACENT ally spending its whole activation gets it back. The wall runs the full height
# of the board with one gap at the top, so the two halves are about fourteen steps apart:
# Player A's three units can afford to lose one to a pit, and Player B's single Threadcaster
# cannot, because nobody can walk to it in time.

id: hz-long-way-round
number: 205
name: The Long Way Round
description: A wall splits the board and the only gap is at the top. Three units on one side can pull each other out; the one unit on the other side gets no second chance.

spawn h = Husk
spawn s = Stalker

footing: Stalker=1

roster a: Vanguard, Archer, Wardbearer
roster b: Threadcaster

board:
  ..h.....B
  .O..#...B
  ....#.^OB
  ..s.#..s.
  ....#...H
  AAO.#..O.
  AA.h#...^
